{title: New Every Morning}
{subtitle: Lamentations 3:22–24}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]city walls lay broken and the gates [Eb]were black with flame
I [Gm]sat among the ashes and I [Eb]could not speak his name
I [Bb]tasted only wormwood and I [Eb]swallowed only gall
My [Gm]soul remembered every wound and [Eb]sank beneath it all
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Yet this I call [Gm]to mind
[Eb]And therefore I have [Bb]hope
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD's acts [Bbmaj7/A]of [Gm]mercy never [Eb]cease
His compas[Bb]sions never come to an [F]end
They are [Eb]new every morn[Bb]ing
Great [Gm]is your faithful[F]ness
The [Eb]LORD is my [Bb]portion, says my [Gm]soul
[Eb]Therefore I will [F]hope in him [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The grey light finds the window and the dark [Eb]begins to fade
The [Gm]night that I was dreading is a night [Eb]that he has made
I [Bb]did not earn the morning and I [Eb]could not pay the cost
But [Gm]mercy came to find me in the pla[Eb]ces I had lost
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Pre-Chorus (repeat)}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The LORD's acts [F/A]of [Gm]mercy never [Eb]cease
His compas[Bb]sions never come to an [F]end
They [Eb]are new every [Bb]morning
Great [Gm]is your faithful[F]ness
The [Eb]LORD is my [Bb]portion, says my [Gm]soul
[Eb]Therefore I will [F]hope in [Bb]him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]The LORD is good to those who [Gm]wait for [F]him
[Eb]To the soul [Gm]that seeks [F]him
[Eb]It is good to wait in [Gm]si[F]lence
[Eb]For the salvation of the [F]LORD
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
They [Eb]are new every [Bb]morning
Great [Gm]is your faithful[F]ness
{end_of_verse}

